## Recursive Bubble Sort

### 📌 Problem Description
Implement the Bubble Sort algorithm using recursion to sort an array of integers in ascending order. Instead of using nested loops, the algorithm recursively performs passes to move the largest element to its correct position.

### 💡 Approach
1. Check if the array contains only one element. If so, it is already sorted.
2. Traverse the array and compare adjacent elements.
3. Swap adjacent elements if they are in the wrong order.
4. After one complete pass, the largest element reaches its correct position at the end.
5. Recursively call the function for the remaining unsorted portion of the array.
6. Repeat until the entire array is sorted.

### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis
- **Best Case:** O(n²) for the basic implementation; O(n) if optimized with a swap flag.
- **Average Case:** O(n²)
- **Worst Case:** O(n²)
- **Space Complexity:** O(n) due to recursive call stack space.

### 🛠️ Language
Java

### 🎯 Key Concept
Recursive Bubble Sort demonstrates how an iterative sorting algorithm can be implemented using recursion by reducing the problem size after every pass.


###Solution

class Solution {
    public int[] bubbleSort(int[] nums) {
        // Base case: An array of size 0 or 1 is already sorted
        if (nums == null || nums.length <= 1) {
            return nums;
        }
        
        // Start the recursive sorting process for the entire array length
        bubbleSortRecursive(nums, nums.length);
        return nums;
    }
    
    private void bubbleSortRecursive(int[] nums, int n) {
        // Base case: If the size of the subarray to check is 1, return
        if (n == 1) {
            return;
        }
        
        // One pass of bubble sort: push the largest element in nums[0..n-1] to the end
        for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
            if (nums[i] > nums[i + 1]) {
                // Swap nums[i] and nums[i+1]
                int temp = nums[i];
                nums[i] = nums[i + 1];
                nums[i + 1] = temp;
            }
        }
        
        // Largest element is fixed at the end, now recurse for the remaining n-1 elements
        bubbleSortRecursive(nums, n - 1);
    }
}

